<title>PHILIPPINES: Security Bank owners okay capital hike.</title>
<headline>Security Bank owners okay capital hike.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Security Bank of the Philippines said on Monday its shareholders have approved an increase in authorised capital to 4.5 billion pesos from the present 2.0 billion pesos.</p>
<p>A stockholders' meeting also approved a one-for-2.5 stock rights offer to cover the increase, the bank said in a statement to the Philippine Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Shareholders as of October 31 are eligible to buy the new shares at 25 pesos per share. Shares were being traded on Monday at 66.50 pesos.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
